    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by the elite speed-category utility of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.13), our highest-rated starter. Despite a 45% rain risk, the combination of a favorable park factor (+16%) and a starter in Baz who is highly susceptible to the stolen base (+4% situational boost) makes **Pete Crow-Armstrong** a must-start priority. **Trea Turner** (79.76) and **Kyle Schwarber** (78.41) follow close behind; both benefit immensely from a soft matchup against Abbott, who carries a weak 5.07 xERA. The matchup against the lefty Abbott allows **Kyle Schwarber** to maximize his xwOBA efficiency, while **Trea Turner** remains our premier weapon for both runs and the stolen base category.\n\nOn the platoon front, **Colt Keith** (69.48) and **Christian Yelich** (69.29) provide excellent stability, both benefiting from dynamic platoon advantages against their respective right-handed opponents. While **Yordan Alvarez** (52.37) sees his raw projection dip due to a brutal matchup against the 3.11 xERA of Alvarez, his elite 0.479 xwOBA keeps him in the lineup as a necessary ceiling play. We navigated a tight bench decision with **Chase Meidroth** (52.53), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While **Chase Meidroth** performed respectably against Tolle, the optimizer favored the higher cumulative efficiency of **Carson Benge** (55.45) and the core starters, as we remain disciplined in our game cap management. **Dillon Dingler** (48.66) and **Kazuma Okamoto** (52.14) round out the squad; **Kazuma Okamoto** is a particular point of focus today, as favorable winds are expected to provide a +5% boost to his power potential against McDonald.",
